  "Frente al puerto de Niiza, sus dos columnas de piedra parecen un portal gigante.": "A place off the coast of Niiza Port with two rock pillars that resemble a massive gate.",
  "Fruta azul que crece en climas cálidos y húmedos. Suele consumirse en conserva.": "A vivid-blue fruit that thrives in hot, humid climates. It is popular as a preserved food.",
  "Fruta con hojas, común en el este. Tiene un sabor rico, pero madura pronto y se vuelve muy amarga.": "A leafy fruit commonly found in the east. It has a refined flavor but spoils quickly, turning bitter.",
  "Fruta del bosque, dulce y nutritiva. La fibra de sus hojas también se puede aprovechar.": "A fruit that grows wildly in forests. It is sweet and highly nutritious. Its leaf fiber can also be harvested.",
  "Fruta enorme de sabor intenso y amargo. Se suele preservar con miel.": "A massive fruit. It is exceptionally fragrant with a slightly bitter taste. It is often preserved in honey.",
  "Fruta picante con un aroma dulce que crece en el noroeste de Dagda. Se usa como amuleto de la suerte.": "A spicy fruit with a sweet aroma. Grows in northwest Dagda. It is commonly used as a lucky charm.",
  "Fruta silvestre que crece en árboles de toda Dagda. Se suele usar para preparar ghosh.": "A fruit that grows wildly on tree trunks throughout Dagda. It is typically used to make ghosh.",
  "Fruto amargo de una planta que crece a grandes altitudes. Se suele confundir con el bifruto, que es venenoso.": "A pleasantly bitter plant that thrives in high altitudes. It is often mistaken for the toxic tew fruit.",
  "Fruto comestible de un árbol común en zonas de secano. Suele emplearse para obtener aceite.": "A widespread, drought-resistant plant. Its edible fruit is often squeezed and processed into oil.",
  "Fruto de Noa": "Noa Fruit",
  "Fruto de una planta que se adapta a casi cualquier entorno. Se suele machacar para emplearlo como condimento.": "A plant that can grow almost anywhere. Its fruit is often crushed and used as accent flavoring.",
  "Fruto dulce y resistente a la sequía del desierto. Desecado, se conserva de maravilla.": "A sweet, drought-resistant fruit that thrives in the desert. It preserves excellently when dried.",
  "Fruto inusual que se da mayormente en la región central de Dagda. Los más grandes tienen un sabor más intenso.": "An unusual fruit that grows mainly in central Dagda. Its flavor is known to deepen as it grows in size.",
  "Fruto típico de Twalinn que se recolecta sacudiendo el árbol en el que crece.": "Nuts sold in Twalinn village, gathered by shaking a variety of tree that only grows in certain places.",
  "Frutos cultivados ampliamente en el sur. Contienen granos que, una vez tostados, se venden en varias regiones.": "Berries widely cultivated in the south. The seeds can be removed and roasted then traded as coffee in various regions.",
